          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "For an isomerisation reaction $A \\rightleftharpoons B$, the temperature dependence of equilibrium constant is given by\r\n$\\log _e K=4.0-\\frac{2000}{T}$\r\nThe value of $\\Delta S^{\\circ}$ at Hook is, therefore",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "W2sXR",
              "text": "\r\n$4 R$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "DYnVF",
              "text": "\r\n$5 R$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "rdc8Y",
              "text": "\r\n$400 R$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "aoege",
              "text": "\r\n$2000 R$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "van't Hoff equation giving variation of equilibrium constant, $K$ with temperature $T$ is\r\n$\\log _e K=-\\frac{\\Delta H^{\\circ}}{R T}+\\frac{\\Delta S^{\\circ}}{R}$\r\nGiven, $\\quad \\log _e K=-\\frac{2000}{T}+4.0$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\Delta S^{\\circ} / R=4 \\Rightarrow \\Delta S^{\\circ}=4 R$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
