          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "The reaction, $\\mathrm{SO}_{2}+\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ is\r\nexothermic and reversible. A mixture of $\\mathrm{SO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})$, $\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})$ and $\\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}(\\mathrm{l})$ is at equilibrium in a closed container. Now a certain quantity of extra $\\mathrm{SO}_{2}$ is introduced into the container, the volume remaining the same. Which of the following is/are true?",
            "image": null
